   "subject": "Auxiliary - The 'model' argument must be a character vector of lavaan syntax or a parameter",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, <div><br></div><div>I was trying to use the Auxiliary function to compare its results to analyses previously run with MI. I can&#39;t get my head around this error: </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> auxiliary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aux </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aux</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fun </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;sem&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">The</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;model&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> argument must be a character vector of lavaan syntax </span><span style=\"color:#008\">or</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a parameter table</span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>So here is my code. The dataset is read using the function foreign (originally SPSS dataset) </div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">auxvars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;T3CamCont&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;T3RelIntensity&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;T3PolOr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;T3PolInt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>(auxvars is in fact longer but regardless of length the error is the same) <br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">fit6 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">COS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pan3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> estimator </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ML&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> missing </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;fiml&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fitsemaux </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">auxiliary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aux </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> auxvars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> estimator</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ML&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> missing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;FIML&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div></div><div>which produces the error quoted above.</div><div><br>Any help would be appreciated.</div><div>Thanks</div><div>Giovanni </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "aXNMWkFiDgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
