   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Terrence,<div>Thanks so very much for this -- now it makes sense! I&#39;ll test and report in case of problems. </div><div>And thanks for the tip, this shouldn&#39;t be an issue as I was already using the syntax and the labels to fit invariance.  </div><div>Best, </div><div>Giovanni </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, 21 April 2017 12:28:04 UTC+1, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">fit6 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">COS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pan3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> estimator </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ML&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> missing </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;fiml&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fitsemaux </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">auxiliary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aux </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> auxvars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> estimator</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ML&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> missing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;FIML&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></code></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Hi Giovanni, I know you are using the latest development version of semTools since we&#39;ve been in contact about<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> runMI() </font>:-)  If you take a look at the<span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"> ?auxiliary </span>help page, you will see that<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> auxiliary() </font>only accepts a character vector or parameter table, not a previously fitted lavaan object as in previous versions of semTools (that introduces too many potential problems).  So this should work fine:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">fitsemaux </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">auxiliary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">COS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pan3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aux </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> auxvars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">The estimator and missing arguments are unnecessary because they are implied by the use of</span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> auxiliary()</font>.</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">FYI, since you are fitting invariance models, be aware that if you constrain measurement parameters using the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> group.equal </font>argument, then<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> &quot;intercepts&quot; </font>will also constrain the intercepts (means) of auxiliaries and<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> &quot;residuals&quot; </font>will also constrain the variances of auxiliaries, because those keywords operate on any observed (non-latent, non-exogenous) variables in the model.  So the invariance models will be too restrictive and result in Type I errors.</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Until I figure out a way to get around the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> group.equal </font>issue, the way to avoid this problem is to apply equality constraints in the syntax instead, by giving parameters the same label.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427296217000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26NhTGB0DQzHR8I-f1CTef\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
